import H0mework.NavierStokes.EndpointWork.HighFrequencyPhysicalRateReduction

/-!
# Global high-frequency exhaustion generated by a positive endpoint atom

The pointwise radius response is promoted here to a source-owned global
alternative.  A positive endpoint atom produces exactly one of:

* cofinally unbounded least crossing cores, all carrying the faithful-zero
  reciprocal-component forcing law;
* a concrete nonzero gluing residual with its native next/trace and positive
  tangent payment;
* an eventual bounded-core tail which, at every larger requested scale,
  generates an atom-scale high-frequency aggregate and its same-event
  physical rate obstruction.

Thus the finite-core escape is no longer a per-radius loophole.  If it does
not form a genuine cofinal scale lineage, the source itself generates one of
the two physical consumers.  The caller supplies only the actual endpoint
lineage and stage.
-/

